            <div xml:id="d502">

                <pb facs="0687" n="597" sameAs="frus:frus1934v03/pg597"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.825/22: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Cunningham</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-12-14T13:00:00-05:00">December 14, 1931—1
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your December 11, 5 p.m. Congress has left to the several States the general
                    power to regulate pilotage. See revised statutes Section 4235.</p>
                <p>Under respective State laws pilotage required in principal United States ports
                    for all vessels engaged in foreign trade.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
